    "status": "present",
    "value": "Count starting positions that can reach the last index by alternating the specified odd minimum-greater-or-equal and even maximum-less-or-equal jumps; break equal-value ties by smallest index. The approach is: value/index sorting plus monotone stacks construct exact jumps; backward parity reachability. Its target cost is O(n log n) time/O(n) space. Treat the invariant underlying that approach as the reason each local update preserves the required result. Check it against an independent bounded reference before relying on large-domain constructions."
  },
